  ],
  "quest.360F0A0299C21CFB.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.3C75E2453412DC17.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.4E0679061753958F.title": "&d◆ &f&lCombat, Movement & Equipment&r",
  "chapter.4E0679061753958F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Practice first · Epic Fight, ParCool, weapons and accessories"
  ],
  "quest.1C337DAAB88F3340.title": "&f&lBuild a loadout you can use&r",
  "quest.1C337DAAB88F3340.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fThe selected pack combines Epic Fight, Weapons of Miracles, Simply Swords, Iron’s spells, movement tools and the personal skilltree. Read the controls and test one complete loadout before taking it into a boss arena.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fChange one equipment piece at a time when comparing builds.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1C337DAAB88F3340.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.20C3D934E20FE40D.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.2E8028D749E2E6C6.title": "&f&lUse the training yard&r",
  "quest.2E8028D749E2E6C6.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fUse a safe target to compare attacks, recovery, mana cost and movement. A dummy can help with controlled comparisons, but a stationary target does not reproduce a boss’s movement or resistance.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fRepeat the same short attack sequence with both loadouts.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.2E8028D749E2E6C6.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.3F081CEA53817741.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.1CE405E9A5BA51B5.title": "&f&lLearn your weapon moves&r",
  "quest.1CE405E9A5BA51B5.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fEpic Fight and its weapon addons can give different weapons distinct attacks. Check battle-mode controls and the actual weapon’s supported moves rather than assuming every weapon handles alike.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fReserve room around the target while learning an unfamiliar combo.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1CE405E9A5BA51B5.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.73D1DC4E7A2D272F.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.5E9FA02AABB379C7.title": "&f&lPractice a clean escape&r",
  "quest.5E9FA02AABB379C7.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fParCool adds movement options with their own controls and conditions. Practice on a safe course, check your available movement resources and learn a route back to solid ground.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest ladders, ledges and recovery in town before attempting the same movement over a dangerous drop.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5E9FA02AABB379C7.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.32E964C0F6741601.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.7D0264CAB9C5D11C.title": "&f&lArmor and tradeoffs&r",
  "quest.7D0264CAB9C5D11C.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fCompare armor, durability, affixes and effects with your class penalties. A damage-focused subclass may give up health or armor; a casting build may need mana or regeneration as much as raw attack damage.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fDo not discard a useful lower-rarity item merely because the replacement has a brighter name.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.7D0264CAB9C5D11C.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.479959851996790D.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.589A1BB4EA0D3A88.title": "&f&lCurios, Artifacts and Relics&r",
  "quest.589A1BB4EA0D3A88.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fArtifacts, Relics and their selected integrations add equipment with their own activation and upgrade rules. Read their tooltips and inspect Curios slots. Carry a few useful effects instead of assuming every found item works from the main inventory.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest the effect in a safe area and check any charge, cooldown or unlock condition.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.589A1BB4EA0D3A88.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.6966F7974CA62C25.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.675C3FE616093E19.title": "&f&lGrowing a relic&r",
  "quest.675C3FE616093E19.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fReliquified Artifacts, Ars Nouveau and Twilight Forest extend the corresponding equipment systems. Follow the actual relic’s progression screen and requirements; an item discovery and a fully developed relic are different goals.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fBuild around a relic you can use regularly, and note which activities advance its own requirements.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.675C3FE616093E19.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.77ABAA845DDA3BEF.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.6EFB94431D3C9828.title": "&f&lAffixes, gems and enchanting&r",
  "quest.6EFB94431D3C9828.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fApotheosis and the selected Apothic systems add equipment and enchanting layers. Inspect affixes, sockets and the relevant workstation recipes in JEI before modifying a favorite item.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fUse spare equipment to learn a workstation’s behavior before committing your best gear.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6EFB94431D3C9828.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.7E3144F242DDF584.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.5EDB4FE3B0656618.title": "&f&lPrepare a recovery kit&r",
  "quest.5EDB4FE3B0656618.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fKeep spare food, tools, blocks and a return plan at home. Shared quest progress does not remove the need to recover from an expedition that goes wrong.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fMake the kit accessible to teammates who may help you return.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5EDB4FE3B0656618.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.2FC3827D62009215.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.195A7CF1722F738B.title": "&d◆ &f&lAutomation Workshop&r",
  "chapter.195A7CF1722F738B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Materials → mechanism → casing → machine · build reliable supply lines"
  ],
  "quest.361CFFD75A6AFDD5.title": "&f&lA factory starts with the flow&r",
  "quest.361CFFD75A6AFDD5.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fPlan every line from raw input to useful output. Give each step its machine, power, ingredient buffer and collection point. Chapters I–X provide the recipes; this page helps make those recipes run continuously.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest one batch before connecting a large farm or bulk storage buffer.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.361CFFD75A6AFDD5.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.5708A0649E1BC0E9.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.5C18E21ED6A34AC6.title": "&f&lRotation, speed and stress&r",
  "quest.5C18E21ED6A34AC6.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fCreate machinery needs a connected rotating network. Speed changes can also change stress requirements. Inspect the machine and network feedback before adding more equipment or gearing up.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fWhen a line stalls, check the output, rotation and stress status before rebuilding the recipe.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5C18E21ED6A34AC6.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.462465B2F7C20959.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.1F33C1297940DB17.title": "&f&lBuild the assembly in order&r",
  "quest.1F33C1297940DB17.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fT&K3 mechanisms use one-loop sequenced assembly. Put the base onto a belt or depot and carry it through the operations in the recipe’s exact order. The Kinetic Mechanism starts from a wooden slab, receives Andesite Alloy twice and finishes under an iron hammer.",
    "",
    "&6&l◇ HOW TO&r",
    "&61. &fStock each operation from a labelled buffer.",
    "&62. &fPlace the listed finishing tool in the last Deployer.",
    "&63. &fRun one complete item and inspect the finished output.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fA wrong ingredient or skipped operation leaves an incomplete item instead of a finished mechanism.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1F33C1297940DB17.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.070E4C42A48910BB.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.3FA4B67FEEA86782.title": "&f&lTools need a supply plan&r",
  "quest.3FA4B67FEEA86782.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fOrdinary finishing tools wear during assembly. Chapter rewards replace that maintenance with a named unbreakable version per player. Until then, keep an accessible replacement buffer and inspect the final Deployer when production stops.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep combat tools out of the automatic ingredient feed.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.3FA4B67FEEA86782.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.4E2B773CCFBB8A19.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.7EBC9C739384C57D.title": "&f&lDeploy the mechanism onto its casing&r",
  "quest.7EBC9C739384C57D.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fA machine frame is assembled by deploying its mechanism onto the matching casing. Stonecutting then turns a frame into a selected machine. It consumes that frame, so a list of stonecut outputs is a menu of separate choices.",
    "",
    "&6&l◇ HOW TO&r",
    "&61. &fProduce the correct casing.",
    "&62. &fDeploy its matching mechanism.",
    "&63. &fStonecut the frame into the machine you need.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fOnly the first Kinetic Machine has the expensive raw-material startup shortcut.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.7EBC9C739384C57D.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.5BE97F6179188A46.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.308D66077A414141.title": "&f&lRenewable stone and elements&r",
  "quest.308D66077A414141.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBuild a water/lava cobblestone or stone generator. Place the selector directly below the newly generated block and its correct frame one block below the selector. The custom generator changes the new stone into the selected geological block.",
    "",
    "&6&l◇ HOW TO&r",
    "&61. &fChoose a row from the wiki’s generator table.",
    "&62. &fPlace selector and frame in the two blocks below the generation position.",
    "&63. &fRun the generator and collect its output.",
    "&64. &fMill the early material or crush it once Chapter III is available.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fA missing selector or wrong frame gives the ordinary generator result. Obsidian remains obsidian.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.308D66077A414141.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.226EFEF23DA235A3.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.181EC0E543D426FD.title": "&f&lGive each stone a destination&r",
  "quest.181EC0E543D426FD.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fAndesite supplies clay, Diorite quartz, Granite lapis and Limestone bone meal. Veridium supplies copper and Crimsite iron. In Brass, Scoria supplies redstone, Scorchia coal, Asurine zinc and Ochrum gold. Milling and crushing have their own listed yields.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep the generator’s raw output apart from processed dusts and metals. Crushing Wheels start in Chapter III.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.181EC0E543D426FD.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.6031AFC1E3F35873.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.4D9BC82EAF764CBA.title": "&f&lA renewable wood line&r",
  "quest.4D9BC82EAF764CBA.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fA Create tree farm needs harvesting, sapling supply, replanting and output transfer. Plan each job before scaling the contraption. Supported wood processing cuts logs into stripped logs, then six planks.",
    "",
    "&6&l◇ HOW TO&r",
    "&61. &fTest the selected tree type on a small area.",
    "&62. &fAdd harvesting and replanting.",
    "&63. &fTransfer the harvest into a wood buffer.",
    "&64. &fSend only the needed logs into processing.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep a protected sapling reserve so downstream crafting cannot eat the next planting batch.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.4D9BC82EAF764CBA.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.0B17B84B5AEF0D98.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.283B33242F7C7681.title": "&f&lWheat and kelp become slime&r",
  "quest.283B33242F7C7681.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fThe authored mixer route uses one wheat, one kelp and 250 mB water to produce two slimeballs. Slime and dried kelp then feed Rubber Compound, making the early sealing line renewable.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fPump water into a dedicated buffer and keep surplus wheat available for food.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.283B33242F7C7681.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 2+",
  "task.586264CFFBD0A0E7.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.6631F964A35480EC.title": "&f&lFans and processing conditions&r",
  "quest.6631F964A35480EC.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fWashing, haunting and other fan processes depend on the correct fan setup and recipe. Use JEI and Ponder to check the required medium and placement. Do not assume every crushed item has a washing result.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fFilter the output and test one item before attaching the entire ore store.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6631F964A35480EC.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.53428DF7FCC11501.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.35991A6495F991A9.title": "&f&lSlice & Dice in the kitchen&r",
  "quest.35991A6495F991A9.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fThe Slicer automates supported Farmer’s Delight cutting recipes with the appropriate held knife. The Sprinkler belongs to the field-and-fluid tier. Inspect the actual supported cutting recipe and water arrangement before scaling.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fPut a knife replacement plan next to the kitchen ingredients.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.35991A6495F991A9.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 2+",
  "task.767865819D34B803.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.5DF56A263A761E2A.title": "&f&lStorage on a contraption&r",
  "quest.5DF56A263A761E2A.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fThe selected Sophisticated integrations connect storage and backpacks to Create systems. Test the supported inventory on a small contraption and confirm which upgrades and transfers work there.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fVerify that cargo leaves the moving inventory before extending the farm.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5DF56A263A761E2A.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.07D8B4BC1E7FA2FF.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.773322A64003CBA0.title": "&f&lLiquid experience and enchantments&r",
  "quest.773322A64003CBA0.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fEnchantment Industry gives experience-processing equipment and its native enchanting rules. Use the Chapter V routes, keep XP apart from water and other fluids, and check the selected recipe for the desired operation.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fA liquid XP supply does not make every enchantment free or remove native requirements.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.773322A64003CBA0.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 5+",
  "task.7A88332BF738CCBC.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.5AB9B90A9F1BA41F.title": "&f&lBuffers before clever logistics&r",
  "quest.5AB9B90A9F1BA41F.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fUse small input buffers, exact filters and a visible overflow plan. Brass-tier logistics can supply requested ingredients, but they still need available stock and working transfers.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fA buffer near the machine makes it easier to see whether the failure is production or transport.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5AB9B90A9F1BA41F.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 3+",
  "task.44C85A1893B004D8.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.381B4AA20F1A6756.title": "&f&lRun a useful line unattended&r",
  "quest.381B4AA20F1A6756.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fChoose one renewable workshop material. Connect resource production, processing and storage, then let several complete batches run without hand-feeding ingredients.",
    "",
    "&6&l◇ HOW TO&r",
    "&61. &fChoose an alloy, mechanism, crop or wood line.",
    "&62. &fAdd filters and input reserves.",
    "&63. &fTest repeated batches and output collection.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fInspect the line again when the output buffer is nearly full.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.381B4AA20F1A6756.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.29A57BB898F6D129.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.7DE09D2C015CFAC9.title": "&d◆ &f&lPower & Digital Logistics&r",
  "chapter.7DE09D2C015CFAC9.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Chapter IV onward · Mekanism, AE2 and Applied Mekanistics"
  ],
  "quest.1289DCCC86D7A75C.title": "&f&lThree systems, three jobs&r",
  "quest.1289DCCC86D7A75C.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fCreate rotation runs the mechanical workshop. FE powers electric machinery. AE2 stores items and coordinates crafting. Mekanism chemicals add another material layer; a power cable is not a chemical pipe.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fBuild a small working example of each connection before combining them.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1289DCCC86D7A75C.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.1A243C10BA252B88.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.50B5B94F7ED14460.title": "&f&lStart electric power with precision&r",
  "quest.50B5B94F7ED14460.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fChapter IV begins with heated steel, Steel Casing and Precision Mechanisms. These bootstrap powered processing, a Heat Generator, basic cables, the AE2 Charger and Inscriber before the Inductive Machine exists.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fFollow Chapter IV’s order to avoid planning a machine that needs the component it is supposed to produce.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.50B5B94F7ED14460.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE · TIER 4+",
  "task.67AC8A4CB17EA5A1.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.5AC989DDD1CACD30.title": "&f&lConfigure inputs and outputs&r",
  "quest.5AC989DDD1CACD30.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fMekanism machines have side and transfer settings. Give energy, items and chemicals the appropriate connections, then verify a single operation. Upgrading a machine is not a substitute for configuring it.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fIf the recipe is correct but no progress starts, inspect the machine’s energy and side screens.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5AC989DDD1CACD30.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 4+",
  "task.742C2A905576FF55.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.53DF5123BEF237D9.title": "&f&lYour first ME network&r",
  "quest.53DF5123BEF237D9.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBegin with power input, a terminal, a drive and a small storage cell. Add automation only after you can insert and retrieve materials reliably. The native network’s energy and channel rules still apply.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep frequently used ingredients in the network and a small recovery reserve outside it.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.53DF5123BEF237D9.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 4+",
  "task.11808C15C3C6DB35.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.25098AA3D74F4364.title": "&f&lTeach a process, then request it&r",
  "quest.25098AA3D74F4364.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fAutocrafting needs a valid pattern, a supported execution device and somewhere for the result to return. Distinguish a crafting pattern from a processing recipe that runs in an external machine.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest a single requested batch with empty machine inputs before building many parallel interfaces.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.25098AA3D74F4364.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 4+",
  "task.1E84D9C66AD85938.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.27A59A50EAF3186E.title": "&f&lUpgrades preserve what matters&r",
  "quest.27A59A50EAF3186E.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fThe managed storage and factory upgrades retain their native component-preserving recipe behavior. Use the supported upgrade route to keep stored contents and configuration rather than substituting an arbitrary shaped recipe.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fMake a backup before testing major inventory upgrades on your main world.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.27A59A50EAF3186E.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.0901C2CF0DB91176.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.01CD0634E3143F0C.title": "&f&lChemical storage is its own layer&r",
  "quest.01CD0634E3143F0C.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fApplied Mekanistics adds chemical network storage alongside AE2. Chapter VI introduces the managed chemical housing and native preserving cell upgrades. Use compatible chemical storage and transfers rather than putting a gas into an item cell.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep each chemical line labelled. Hydrogen, chlorine and hydrogen chloride have different jobs.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.01CD0634E3143F0C.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 6+",
  "task.509410106AD94E39.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.01EFDAD513378219.title": "&f&lFeed only what a machine needs&r",
  "quest.01EFDAD513378219.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fKeep background production and on-demand production distinct. A permanent supply line can fill a buffer; a request-based line should return precisely the expected result to the network.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fReserve some basic materials so a request does not consume all of your startup stock.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.01EFDAD513378219.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 6+",
  "task.1ACDD8FD9B60D965.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.753778B35B2202D2.title": "&f&lA remote factory still needs service&r",
  "quest.753778B35B2202D2.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fWireless and quantum links help with remote storage access, but their native energy, range, channel and linking rules remain. Remote machines also need working world loading under your instance’s settings.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest insertion, retrieval and production while you are away from the workshop.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.753778B35B2202D2.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 9+",
  "task.6169A7A8ACDE6C8C.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.09CD36F42C1C3A38.title": "&d◆ &f&lRoutes, Rails & Airships&r",
  "chapter.09CD36F42C1C3A38.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A connected kingdom · Brass transport and Integrated expeditions"
  ],
  "quest.19998A9E3AE0C0AE.title": "&f&lChoose the route for the job&r",
  "quest.19998A9E3AE0C0AE.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fRoads, Create transport, Hypertubes, Waystones and Aeronautics serve different kinds of travel and cargo. Plan stations and delivery inventories before adding long routes.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fStart with a short route between two known inventories or safe landing points.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.19998A9E3AE0C0AE.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.3B9EC1E6CE4EB207.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.2E556C559FF76986.title": "&f&lTest a short Hypertube route&r",
  "quest.2E556C559FF76986.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fChapter III supplies precision-based entrances and accelerators alongside native tube sections. Build a short accessible route, supply its required power and test both ends before extending it.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fLeave room around entrances so you can service the route.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.2E556C559FF76986.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 3+",
  "task.087084DF0BB2640A.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.69796A731256F7AA.title": "&f&lGive a route a useful cargo job&r",
  "quest.69796A731256F7AA.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fUse Create’s supported transport components and Ponder to plan track, stations and cargo handling. Tie each destination to a real buffer, such as crop delivery or timber collection.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fConfirm unloading before adding another stop.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.69796A731256F7AA.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 3+",
  "task.3A72E4FEDA4D52DF.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.0202FA2010A3901E.title": "&f&lSupply the colony through the workshop&r",
  "quest.0202FA2010A3901E.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fCreate: MineColonies Link is selected to connect workshop logistics with colony requests. Inspect the installed link’s supported blocks and in-game guidance, then test one requested material with a small supply.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fGive the colony a dedicated buffer so settlement demand does not consume the entire mechanism line.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.0202FA2010A3901E.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 3+",
  "task.130E6559207C3F92.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.752F5687616074DF.title": "&f&lBuild the first expedition vessel&r",
  "quest.752F5687616074DF.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fChapter VII introduces Expedition Frames for Aeronautics controls. Plan a light hull, balanced propulsion, steering, fuel or power, and cargo access. Follow the addon’s actual supported setup.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest turning, stopping and cargo access close to home before crossing a long distance.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.752F5687616074DF.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 7+",
  "task.6599D205EAE34AF9.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.4FEF05079AF54B81.title": "&f&lPower and processing aboard&r",
  "quest.4FEF05079AF54B81.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fAeronautics Mekanism compatibility provides the selected moving-vessel integration. Check which blocks and networks are supported in the installed versions, then test one electric machine aboard before expanding.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fObserve power, inputs and outputs during movement as well as while parked.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.4FEF05079AF54B81.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 7+",
  "task.1BF784D9472C4C6B.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.09F33FC1349B68F4.title": "&f&lTravel and magic aboard&r",
  "quest.09F33FC1349B68F4.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fThe current selection includes Aeronautics integrations for FTB Chunks, Iron’s Spells and Waystones: Sable. Read each installed addon’s supported behavior and settings before relying on claims, spell effects or travel from a moving vessel.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest the exact interaction on a short trip with a safe landing point.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.09F33FC1349B68F4.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 7+",
  "task.1B9B549C8966A8B8.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.73FEDB04B3253A67.title": "&f&lBuild a resupply outpost&r",
  "quest.73FEDB04B3253A67.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fMake a remote stop with fuel or energy, food, storage and repair supplies. Record the approach route and a safe landing area so the next expedition starts prepared.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fLeave an emergency return option for the crew.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.73FEDB04B3253A67.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 7+",
  "task.68DC48E5CB6460ED.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.3DA2623620D25F39.title": "&d◆ &f&lArs Nouveau · The Living Workshop&r",
  "chapter.3DA2623620D25F39.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Spells, Source and magical automation alongside the factory"
  ],
  "quest.217B1848E6453CAD.title": "&f&lLearn Ars on its own terms&r",
  "quest.217B1848E6453CAD.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fArs Nouveau combines a spellbook, glyphs, Source and automation devices. Use its in-game guide and JEI together. Your class’s Iron’s spell attributes do not automatically describe every Ars spell or Source device.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fStart with one useful spell and one reliable Source supply.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.217B1848E6453CAD.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.0026839E2A19D617.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.04959E0FC9641AD0.title": "&f&lA first spellbook&r",
  "quest.04959E0FC9641AD0.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fFollow the native spellbook recipe and upgrade requirements shown in JEI. Read the guide’s instructions for making and editing a spell, then test a simple combination in a safe area.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep spell testing away from crops, settlers and important machine rooms.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.04959E0FC9641AD0.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.5D290B22A84A7B4A.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.0FE3519293895ABD.title": "&f&lRead glyphs before combining them&r",
  "quest.0FE3519293895ABD.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fGlyphs describe how a spell starts, what it does and how it is modified. Inspect the available glyphs and their costs before building a complicated sequence.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fA short spell whose effects you understand is easier to improve.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.0FE3519293895ABD.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.4C37871DCB505365.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.447275F4492FB0AC.title": "&f&lSource is a production supply&r",
  "quest.447275F4492FB0AC.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fSourcelinks generate Source under their own conditions and jars hold it for supported devices. The Chapter IV Agronomic Sourcelink bootstrap uses wheat, Source Gems, a Source Jar and a Precision Machine.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep Source generation close enough to the actual consumers under Ars’s native transfer rules.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.447275F4492FB0AC.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE · TIER 4+",
  "task.2765AE5294FF2D14.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.13BD43BF8BC6197B.title": "&f&lA parallel arcane workshop&r",
  "quest.13BD43BF8BC6197B.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fA Precision Machine bootstraps the Enchanting Apparatus before the custom Arcane Machine. Produce Arcane Casing and its sequenced mechanism, then deploy the mechanism onto the casing. This is a supporting branch alongside electric industry.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fThe Arcane Machine is not a prerequisite for starting the first Source supply.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.13BD43BF8BC6197B.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 4+",
  "task.3ADBB7F3B88E89C5.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.1E65FDD48E0BD757.title": "&f&lHelpers with clear jobs&r",
  "quest.1E65FDD48E0BD757.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fArs automation helpers each have their own binding and task rules. Give a helper one supported job and a visible destination, then test collection before adding more work.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep the output inventory accessible so you can see whether the helper is collecting or stalled.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1E65FDD48E0BD757.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 4+",
  "task.65EBB3D1667E6DEC.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.4640DACA2970A575.title": "&f&lArs Creo · Starbuncle Wheel&r",
  "quest.4640DACA2970A575.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fArs Creo’s Starbuncle Wheel adds a real Ars/Create connection. Follow its native operating rules and Ponder or in-game guide, then test it on a small rotating setup.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fCheck the wheel’s actual operating conditions instead of treating Source as a universal replacement for every power system.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.4640DACA2970A575.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 4+",
  "task.6F6F5EE76C5FC9AC.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.14611BCC84919F75.title": "&f&lCreate and Source together&r",
  "quest.14611BCC84919F75.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fCreate: Ars Nouveau compatibility and Wizardry are selected workshop integrations. Inspect each actual recipe and machine tooltip to see whether the process needs rotation, Source, a spell or more than one system.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fLabel Source connections separately from water, liquid XP and other fluid lines.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.14611BCC84919F75.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 4+",
  "task.11A4343A80C6E2E9.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.51C77A50622FA337.title": "&f&lMagical equipment and relics&r",
  "quest.51C77A50622FA337.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fReliquified Ars Nouveau and Ars ’n Spells extend selected equipment or compatibility systems. Read the item’s own effects and restrictions; an Ars item and an Iron’s spellbook still have distinct rules.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest one supported effect at a time when comparing a hybrid loadout.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.51C77A50622FA337.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.1763775F91921A66.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.3FD9C996C3ED542D.title": "&f&lA living supply line&r",
  "quest.3FD9C996C3ED542D.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBuild one Ars-assisted crop, collection or processing setup whose output feeds the workshop or storehouse. Include Source supply, the helper or device and a collection buffer.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep manual access to the buffer so the team can service the line.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.3FD9C996C3ED542D.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 4+",
  "task.2C460AD889FF8D0D.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.35159DAF2C158BF3.title": "&d◆ &f&lIron’s Spells · The Spellcraft Hall&r",
  "chapter.35159DAF2C158BF3.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Schools, mana, scrolls, jewelry and selected spell addons"
  ],
  "quest.1734C8B9EC584093.title": "&f&lBuild a useful spell loadout&r",
  "quest.1734C8B9EC584093.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fIron’s Spells ’n Spellbooks uses its own spells, schools, mana and equipment. Start with a damage option and a utility or recovery option, then compare their costs and cooldowns.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fYour spell’s actual school matters more than the visual color of its effect.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1734C8B9EC584093.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.5807546990EAD247.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.67564F0CEE5FF10C.title": "&f&lLearn the scroll and book rules&r",
  "quest.67564F0CEE5FF10C.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fUse found or crafted scrolls and the supported spellbook stations according to their native requirements. Inspect rarity, level, slots and prerequisites before committing a valuable scroll.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep a record of the spells you already use so you do not replace a useful utility spell by accident.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.67564F0CEE5FF10C.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.7251DA65A6D73924.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.7A1EDD7FEF5AE53D.title": "&f&lMana, casting time and cooldown&r",
  "quest.7A1EDD7FEF5AE53D.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fMana capacity, regeneration, casting time and cooldown are different limits. A bigger mana pool does not guarantee faster recovery between fights. Read your gear and skill node effects together.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest several casts in succession and watch what becomes the bottleneck.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.7A1EDD7FEF5AE53D.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.0F81544224040E0C.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.27088544AB5A7B7E.title": "&f&lSpecialize by school&r",
  "quest.27088544AB5A7B7E.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fThe current classes support Holy, Blood, Ender, Eldritch, Fire, Ice and Lightning themes in different ways. Read a spell’s tooltip to confirm that it belongs to the school you are building around.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fThe relevant attribute must exist in the installed mod version for a school-specific bonus to apply.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.27088544AB5A7B7E.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.151DFECCE6931DCD.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.58E7B91E9FC3F988.title": "&f&lBrewing and spell supplies&r",
  "quest.58E7B91E9FC3F988.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fThe selected Iron’s KubeJS bridge manages supported cauldron recipes while native spell systems remain. Inspect the exact recipe and fluid requirement in JEI before building a potion or reagent supply.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep brewing inputs and finished bottles in separate storage.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.58E7B91E9FC3F988.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.32917D5C2A8F0874.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.6C6FF048DC8F1A8A.title": "&f&lThe Jewelcrafting Guide&r",
  "quest.6C6FF048DC8F1A8A.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fObtain and read the Jewelcrafting Guide.",
    "",
    "&fIron’s Gems ’n Jewelry keeps its native jewel and component systems. Chapter II supplies the station and guide. Read the actual jewel and component effects before assembling equipment for your class.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fUse the station recipe and guide together; a jewel’s effect depends on the resulting equipment.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6C6FF048DC8F1A8A.quest_subtitle": "&7ITEM GOAL · TIER 2+",
  "quest.5077E82C56904527.title": "&f&lSpells found through adventure&r",
  "quest.5077E82C56904527.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fAlex’s Caves: Spellbooks, Cataclysm: Spellbooks and Twilight Forest: Spellbooks connect magic to their corresponding adventures. Inspect the installed addon’s JEI entries and discovery rules, then choose one spell to pursue.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fLet your current workshop access and combat readiness guide the destination.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5077E82C56904527.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.0FDE42E54708C7D8.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.1ECC89779AD08841.title": "&f&lExpanded spell schools and effects&r",
  "quest.1ECC89779AD08841.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fGeomancy Plus, Archaion: Echoes of the Fallen and Echoing Magic: Esoteric Spells of the Fallen are selected spell additions. Read each spell’s real school, acquisition route and effect. The questbook does not invent an unlock item for these native spells.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fCompare new spells in the training yard before relying on them during a boss fight.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1ECC89779AD08841.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.204CEC55027E84D4.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.6D2BA0F7EF423407.title": "&f&lMatch spellcraft to a class&r",
  "quest.6D2BA0F7EF423407.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fMage favors sustained or elemental casting, Cleric favors Holy and recovery themes, and Occultist favors Blood, summons or void schools. Rogue and Warrior hybrid paths can support specific effects without making every spell a melee bonus.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fRead the class and subclass root penalties before choosing your final equipment.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6D2BA0F7EF423407.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.1CA1835A0B73BCC0.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.516923EFBE3E1099.title": "&f&lA complete spellcraft trial&r",
  "quest.516923EFBE3E1099.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fEquip your chosen book and accessories, test a damage spell and a utility or recovery spell, then finish an ordinary expedition without exhausting your supply plan.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fBring normal food and equipment too; spells are part of the loadout.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.516923EFBE3E1099.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.3E82499543D7BCC1.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.6CC43719B0315F94.title": "&d◆ &f&lWitchery · The Hedge Scholar&r",
  "chapter.6CC43719B0315F94.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Just Another Witchery Remake · native discovery and a careful study journal"
  ],
  "quest.65535A425066AACD.title": "&f&lA different magical tradition&r",
  "quest.65535A425066AACD.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fJust Another Witchery Remake is in the current alpha mod selection. Its magic is a separate branch from Ars Source and Iron’s spellbooks. Use the installed mod’s guide entries and JEI to discover the available systems.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep a dedicated study journal for recipes and prerequisites you have actually found.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.65535A425066AACD.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.0B7C5B188D07472E.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.163048D43E40CDEB.title": "&f&lFind the first native guide&r",
  "quest.163048D43E40CDEB.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fInspect the installed Witchery entries and locate the guide or starter information available in this release. Record one verified starting recipe and its ingredients.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fAddon versions can differ, so follow the guide in your instance.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.163048D43E40CDEB.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.4C186A1073CCA69D.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.601899D9C14CC416.title": "&f&lThe hedge garden&r",
  "quest.601899D9C14CC416.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fChoose a plant or reagent that the installed Witchery recipes use, identify its actual source and grow or gather a renewable supply where the native rules allow it.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fProtect a planting reserve before sending herbs into crafting.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.601899D9C14CC416.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.7F3308BE83883606.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.790074E82FEA916D.title": "&f&lA separate ritual workspace&r",
  "quest.790074E82FEA916D.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fSet aside an accessible area for the native workstations or ritual setups you discover. Follow their actual placement and environment requirements rather than substituting a Create basin or Ars apparatus.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fLeave space to expand without moving the whole workshop.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.790074E82FEA916D.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.33F2BDE29DA0E72C.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.791777E26C131A0D.title": "&f&lDocument one working process&r",
  "quest.791777E26C131A0D.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fChoose a native Witchery process, complete its prerequisites and run it. Write down the input, required setup and result so another player can reproduce it.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fConfirm the result before reserving large quantities of a rare reagent.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.791777E26C131A0D.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.1743ED897A29D20C.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.63AF6B3DE70AC1EB.title": "&f&lA hedge scholar’s contribution&r",
  "quest.63AF6B3DE70AC1EB.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fFind one native Witchery result that is useful to your own adventures or settlement. Prepare its materials, demonstrate the result and add it to the town library’s notes.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fThe activity check records the project; it does not add a custom transformation or ritual unlock.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.63AF6B3DE70AC1EB.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.7B7AEAA546DC7A7D.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.55A1B7272D5521E3.title": "&d◆ &f&lThe Explorer’s Journal&r",
  "chapter.55A1B7272D5521E3.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Worlds, structures, travel and a safe return"
  ],
  "quest.2E1508AF93DE3FC2.title": "&f&lExplore with a purpose&r",
  "quest.2E1508AF93DE3FC2.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fChoose a destination for a useful discovery: crop, building palette, spell, equipment or workshop ingredient. Bring supplies, inventory space and a plan for returning home.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fRecord discoveries you cannot use yet; they may become useful in a later tier.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.2E1508AF93DE3FC2.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.77DC970039ED60B1.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.2A15888BF835CC87.title": "&f&lA world of building palettes&r",
  "quest.2A15888BF835CC87.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBiomes O’ Plenty, Oh The Biomes We’ve Gone, Atmospheric, Environmental, Autumnity and other selected world mods add places and materials to explore. Bring home a palette sample and note its location.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fCheck whether a plant can be grown at home before committing to a long repeat trip.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.2A15888BF835CC87.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.313A6867631C1D43.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.412EE3BCD151D10E.title": "&f&lDiscover a new structure&r",
  "quest.412EE3BCD151D10E.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fIntegrated structures, YUNG’s improvements and the selected dungeon additions create exploration destinations. Approach carefully, identify an exit and distinguish ordinary loot from a boss objective.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fMark the entrance and unfinished rooms on your map.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.412EE3BCD151D10E.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.73DAA5BBFCE7A72B.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.205A3B8314EB0674.title": "&f&lLooting as a team&r",
  "quest.205A3B8314EB0674.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fLootr is selected for supported personal-loot containers. Read the actual container feedback and server settings rather than assuming every chest in the world behaves the same.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fAgree on rules for ordinary shared chests and expedition supplies.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.205A3B8314EB0674.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.5B4CE7D6FFCB8F03.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.1341E6D02D148D4C.title": "&f&lA useful travel stop&r",
  "quest.1341E6D02D148D4C.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fWaystones and the selected Better Party integrations support travel arrangements under their actual settings. Establish a safe stop and check activation, cost and party access before relying on it as the only return route.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fGive destinations clear names that the whole team can recognize.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1341E6D02D148D4C.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.221E51726E4B6D70.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.6C0DD39F1C878FBE.title": "&f&lThe Brass expedition&r",
  "quest.6C0DD39F1C878FBE.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fNether entry begins after Chapter II. Find the ingredients and Blaze access required by the Brass workshop, then record a safe return path. BetterNether and the selected Nether world changes provide further destinations.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fCapture a Blaze in the appropriate burner when preparing heated brass production.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6C0DD39F1C878FBE.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 3+",
  "task.1F9E44C1EFE728AA.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.049F7F0955E03448.title": "&f&lDiscover an Alex’s Cave&r",
  "quest.049F7F0955E03448.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fAlex’s Caves and its selected spell integration offer biome-specific discoveries. Follow their actual guide and discovery mechanics, identify the biome’s hazards and return with one useful finding.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fStock supplies for the conditions of the cave you are visiting.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.049F7F0955E03448.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.352E7E4CFC1D10AC.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.3A390C76D74D0B03.title": "&f&lA bestiary entry&r",
  "quest.3A390C76D74D0B03.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fAlex’s Mobs, Mowzie’s Mobs, Ice & Fire and the selected encounter mods bring creatures with different behaviors. Observe one new creature, read available guidance and record how to approach or avoid it.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fAn unfamiliar creature is not automatically safe because it looks peaceful.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.3A390C76D74D0B03.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.4197E05D37E96FE1.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.6FAED59CCEF3B9ED.title": "&f&lBring the discovery home&r",
  "quest.6FAED59CCEF3B9ED.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fSort an expedition’s haul into food, building materials, gear, magic and progression supplies. Record where rare materials came from so the next trip has a clear purpose.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fLeave room in the incoming-materials area before the team returns with full backpacks.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6FAED59CCEF3B9ED.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.74E4CC4C289BAE50.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.6024F84E209C476E.title": "&d◆ &f&lThe Boss Trial Ledger&r",
  "chapter.6024F84E209C476E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Five permanent campaign catalysts · extra encounters stay optional"
  ],
  "quest.266C9190A20C837E.title": "&f&lKnow which trial matters&r",
  "quest.266C9190A20C837E.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fThe campaign uses Dragon Core, Verdant Sigil, Storm Core, Ember Core and Void Core. Their actual detected kill goals and rewards live in the matching Mechanical chapter. Other bosses remain optional adventures.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fUse this ledger for preparation and the main chapter for the detected kill task.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.266C9190A20C837E.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.5AB9F0D75EEDB58C.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.38CE5C2434B26BA1.title": "&f&lChapter V · The Ender Dragon&r",
  "quest.38CE5C2434B26BA1.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand the trial and prepare for its main-chapter quest.",
    "",
    "&fOpen the End through its native twelve-different-eyes requirement. The detected Dragon trial in Chapter V awards the permanent Dragon Core as a team reward.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fCollect Dragon’s Breath while the fight gives you the opportunity; it supports later processing.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.38CE5C2434B26BA1.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE · TIER 5+",
  "task.615C051F462EFF41.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.79655B61663C7001.title": "&f&lChapter VI · The Twilight Lich&r",
  "quest.79655B61663C7001.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand the trial and prepare for its main-chapter quest.",
    "",
    "&fFollow Twilight Forest’s native progression to the Lich. A player kill gives the reusable Verdant Sigil through the authored loot rule.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fClear the native earlier progression and read the boss’s defenses before starting the fight.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.79655B61663C7001.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE · TIER 6+",
  "task.4A2823AECCCBBB4A.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.6B460A8899F6095C.title": "&f&lChapter VII · The Harbinger&r",
  "quest.6B460A8899F6095C.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand the trial and prepare for its main-chapter quest.",
    "",
    "&fPrepare for Cataclysm’s Harbinger encounter. A player kill gives the reusable Storm Core. Use the chapter’s detected trial to follow campaign progress.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fPrepare your arena approach, recovery supplies and a clear way to retreat before engaging.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6B460A8899F6095C.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE · TIER 7+",
  "task.0343F908568EC7DF.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.62C05A8FFD64B4FB.title": "&f&lChapter VIII · Ignis&r",
  "quest.62C05A8FFD64B4FB.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand the trial and prepare for its main-chapter quest.",
    "",
    "&fPrepare for the native Ignis encounter. A player kill gives the reusable Ember Core; it remains a catalyst for the final imprinting sequence.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fPractice your current weapon and spells before entering the arena with valuable equipment.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.62C05A8FFD64B4FB.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE · TIER 8+",
  "task.4DF6787478E959DD.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.578325F73C5CB9C7.title": "&f&lChapter IX · The Ender Guardian&r",
  "quest.578325F73C5CB9C7.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand the trial and prepare for its main-chapter quest.",
    "",
    "&fThe Ender Guardian’s player-kill drop gives the permanent Void Core. The trial is available before the boss-gated Singularity Frame and supports Void-attuned Singularity production.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fDo not plan the core’s first acquisition around equipment that already needs that core.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.578325F73C5CB9C7.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE · TIER 9+",
  "task.12340C4FE5BBEA77.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.509FDED7F0D4E1F4.title": "&f&lKeep the cores, repeat the production&r",
  "quest.509FDED7F0D4E1F4.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fCore-bearing deployment steps retain their core. The final Sovereign Keystone imprints all five onto a Sovereign Core and finishes with the ordinary Enchanter’s Sword. Repeated boss kills can supply additional parallel catalyst stations.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fStore cores in a labelled secure inventory and keep them out of void or disposal upgrades.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.509FDED7F0D4E1F4.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE · TIER 10+",
  "task.21B9BD2FAE735DDF.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.2494E0F86479D34D.title": "&f&lExtra bosses and discoveries&r",
  "quest.2494E0F86479D34D.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBosses’ Rise, Mowzie’s Mobs, Ice & Fire, Cataclysm and selected structure addons offer more encounters than the five mandatory campaign catalysts. Choose one suitable encounter and document its native reward.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fOptional encounters do not award invented campaign cores.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.2494E0F86479D34D.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.30735D900199791B.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.5F54AB10F9A5CBDB.title": "&d◆ &f&lInto the Twilight Forest&r",
  "chapter.5F54AB10F9A5CBDB.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Native adventure order · Lich catalyst from Chapter VI"
  ],
  "quest.6239A70A4006AE8E.title": "&f&lFollow the forest’s own progression&r",
  "quest.6239A70A4006AE8E.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fTwilight Forest has its own entry and boss progression. Use the native guide, advancements and in-world clues to understand the next destination. The campaign’s Verdant Sigil comes from the Lich player kill.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fA workshop tier does not skip the forest’s earlier native progression requirements.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6239A70A4006AE8E.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.761A76A35F912E27.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.1FC21CCC6EEF58B9.title": "&f&lPrepare the forest journey&r",
  "quest.1FC21CCC6EEF58B9.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fRead the installed portal requirements, bring food and a return plan, and mark your entry location. Leave space for discoveries instead of bringing every workshop tool.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep a spare recovery kit on the home side of the portal.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1FC21CCC6EEF58B9.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.3473FB56589CE802.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.1D46E395C6FADE0E.title": "&f&lYour first forest objective&r",
  "quest.1D46E395C6FADE0E.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fComplete an early native forest objective and read the advancement or guide that explains the next one. Record a route and useful materials for a return visit.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fUse native progression feedback when a biome or boss is inaccessible.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1D46E395C6FADE0E.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.13583233B17ABCB8.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.58943EB584B90C02.title": "&f&lPrepare for the Lich trial&r",
  "quest.58943EB584B90C02.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fComplete the forest’s preceding requirements, find the Lich destination and review your loadout. Chapter VI contains the campaign kill task; its authored player-kill loot gives the Verdant Sigil.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTake a reliable ranged or spell option if your chosen approach needs one.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.58943EB584B90C02.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 6+",
  "task.4807203E5BDFCAD6.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.2E198CD61EF784D5.title": "&f&lForest relics and spellbooks&r",
  "quest.2E198CD61EF784D5.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fThe selected Reliquified Twilight Forest and Twilight Forest: Spellbooks integrations add their own discoveries. Inspect what you actually find and follow each item’s native upgrade or acquisition rules.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep promising equipment even if it suits another teammate’s class better.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.2E198CD61EF784D5.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.0F14032D84ABFC08.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.66C7F3E30E42B2DB.title": "&f&lA reusable forest route&r",
  "quest.66C7F3E30E42B2DB.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fRecord entry, cleared objectives, useful materials and an unfinished destination in the town library. Bring home enough supplies to make the next trip a planned expedition.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fSeparate progression trophies and crafting supplies when sorting the haul.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.66C7F3E30E42B2DB.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.366427A7247DD87A.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.79EFB045B403EA96.title": "&d◆ &f&lBeyond the End Portal&r",
  "chapter.79EFB045B403EA96.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Chapter V · unique eyes, the Dragon and renewable End materials"
  ],
  "quest.037C5A3B2C450C47.title": "&f&lPrepare before crossing&r",
  "quest.037C5A3B2C450C47.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fThe End opens after Chapter IV. End Remastered still requires twelve different valid eyes. Four eyes have authored Inductive Mechanism deployment routes; other unique eyes retain their native discovery sources.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep a list of distinct eye types instead of collecting twelve copies of the same one.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.037C5A3B2C450C47.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.39EC1FD3956616FD.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.0CA94B7CF5EEA189.title": "&f&lTwelve different eyes&r",
  "quest.0CA94B7CF5EEA189.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fInspect the four managed eye deployments in Chapter V and gather the remaining valid types through exploration. Check the portal’s native acceptance rules before committing your collection.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fBuild several exploration goals around eye types you are still missing.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.0CA94B7CF5EEA189.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 5+",
  "task.7EE0A55CA99E981D.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.7060026E8EA9C832.title": "&f&lThe first Dragon expedition&r",
  "quest.7060026E8EA9C832.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fPrepare blocks, food, equipment, free bottle space and a return plan. Follow the detected Chapter V Dragon trial and manually claim its Dragon Core reward after the kill is recorded.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep the core for production; the first core comes from the quest reward rather than a guessed Dragon loot recipe.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.7060026E8EA9C832.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE · TIER 5+",
  "task.4471667E13E2CE97.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.78DCE5B1B11AAE91.title": "&f&lBring back Dragon’s Breath&r",
  "quest.78DCE5B1B11AAE91.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fCollect Dragon’s Breath during the fight. Create: Dragons Plus uses its native breath filling, emptying and ending fan processes, with the managed fluid hatch supporting transport.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep empty bottles ready before the fight and sort the collected breath into its own supply.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.78DCE5B1B11AAE91.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 5+",
  "task.66DE2105C0A284E3.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.6F9E0541FC3D77AA.title": "&f&lGrow the End at home&r",
  "quest.6F9E0541FC3D77AA.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBring chorus supplies and End Stone home, then build a repeatable growing and harvest area. Chorus supports the Ender and chemical workshop layers.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fReserve planting stock before feeding chorus to industrial processing.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6F9E0541FC3D77AA.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 5+",
  "task.68DFFDAF3025BCEB.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.5979654977110DDE.title": "&f&lExplore the End’s new palette&r",
  "quest.5979654977110DDE.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBetterEnd: New Dawn, Nullscape and the selected End changes provide destinations and materials beyond the first island. Plan travel, record routes and bring home a building or crafting discovery.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep a dependable return option before extending a remote exploration route.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5979654977110DDE.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 5+",
  "task.100AE796047B5CAA.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.584E332E61AD4639.title": "&d◆ &f&lOceans & Aquatic Workshops&r",
  "chapter.584E332E61AD4639.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Copper tier · Upgrade Aquatic and Create: Aquatic Ambitions"
  ],
  "quest.69FEFC3A409A70DA.title": "&f&lAn ocean worth exploring&r",
  "quest.69FEFC3A409A70DA.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fUpgrade Aquatic supplies selected aquatic world content. Create: Aquatic Ambitions connects ocean materials to the workshop. Bring breathing and travel supplies appropriate to the actual destination.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fStart with a nearby coast and record useful ocean locations.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.69FEFC3A409A70DA.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.50BB52E0D910F12E.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.459C5A2011841F14.title": "&f&lCalcium-Rich Powder&r",
  "quest.459C5A2011841F14.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fProduce Calcium-Rich Powder for the aquatic metallurgy line.",
    "",
    "&fThe managed mixing route uses bone meal, kelp and water. Keep these inputs available for Prismarine Alloy production and follow the Chapter II metallurgy chain.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fLimestone milling can support the bone-meal buffer.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.459C5A2011841F14.quest_subtitle": "&7ITEM GOAL · TIER 2+",
  "quest.0F153B888AB61037.title": "&f&lPrismarine Alloy&r",
  "quest.0F153B888AB61037.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fProduce the aquatic workshop alloy.",
    "",
    "&fCompact prismarine shard, copper sheet and calcium powder into the managed alloy. Continue through the listed rods and Conduit Cage components rather than assuming every aquatic block shares a vanilla recipe.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fReserve ocean materials for the first cage before spending them on decorations.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.0F153B888AB61037.quest_subtitle": "&7ITEM GOAL · TIER 2+",
  "quest.13E186D8C7E38FDF.title": "&f&lRead the real channeling process&r",
  "quest.13E186D8C7E38FDF.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBuild the managed Conduit Cage and use Aquatic Ambitions’ actual channeling recipes. Its conduit ingredient comes from ocean exploration; the alloy route does not remove that exploration step.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fUse the recipe tab to check each channeling operation’s real requirements.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.13E186D8C7E38FDF.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 2+",
  "task.5D8055B0C7A9A26A.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.61B552308D3CE027.title": "&f&lA coastal supply station&r",
  "quest.61B552308D3CE027.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBuild a safe coastal store with fishing supplies, spare food and space for kelp and ocean materials. Connect a useful resource to the town storehouse.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep a few exploration supplies in the station for the next trip.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.61B552308D3CE027.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.5E7191BC87C2DFD4.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.728AD1163ECEB710.title": "&d◆ &f&lFields, Food & the Kitchen&r",
  "chapter.728AD1163ECEB710.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Farmer’s Delight, Slice & Dice and the selected Let’s Do cooking mods"
  ],
  "quest.6748CF14BADC0D38.title": "&f&lFood and industry share the fields&r",
  "quest.6748CF14BADC0D38.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fYour crops can feed players, colony workers and the factory. Wheat and kelp support slime and seals; later crop processing supplies Bio Fuel. Plan separate food, planting and industrial buffers.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fA factory should receive the surplus, not consume the farm’s last planting materials.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6748CF14BADC0D38.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.45850A7D046C7C20.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.3D65F87E439DA7FF.title": "&f&lA farm with a clear job&r",
  "quest.3D65F87E439DA7FF.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fChoose a crop your team uses and build a small farm with access to water, collection and a planting reserve. Check the crop’s actual growing rules and available harvesting methods.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fMake each field’s destination visible with a sign or labelled chest.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.3D65F87E439DA7FF.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.24F369691847E954.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.41ADAB8492116EA3.title": "&f&lThe useful kelp patch&r",
  "quest.41ADAB8492116EA3.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fKelp feeds Algal Blend, the slime route and aquatic calcium production. Build collection first and keep the factory’s intake separate from a spare growing area.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fThe manual blend route starts your workshop; mixing improves its yield later.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.41ADAB8492116EA3.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.5FD7E76BADC8EE17.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.5FD290A205F7F8BA.title": "&f&lA proper cutting station&r",
  "quest.5FD290A205F7F8BA.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fFarmer’s Delight cutting recipes use their listed tool and output rules. Start with the native board, inspect recipes in JEI and later automate supported cuts with Slice & Dice.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep ingredients and the cutting tool nearby so manual food prep remains easy.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5FD290A205F7F8BA.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.7EE0A33B34A3D2B0.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.5AD93D3CB98E0740.title": "&f&lThe Stove&r",
  "quest.5AD93D3CB98E0740.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fObtain a Stove and prepare a place for the kitchen.",
    "",
    "&fUse Farmer’s Delight’s native cooking setup and recipes to prepare repeatable meals. Plan the input supply and finished-meal storage before adding automatic transfers.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fChoose a meal whose ingredients are already renewable in your settlement.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5AD93D3CB98E0740.quest_subtitle": "&7ITEM GOAL",
  "quest.267D64780256C02B.title": "&f&lMore kitchens, more choices&r",
  "quest.267D64780256C02B.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fFarm & Charm, Bakery, Brewery, Candlelight and BloomingNature add selected farming, food or decoration content. Inspect each mod’s actual recipe stations rather than treating every dish as a Farmer’s Delight pot recipe.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fPick one useful recipe from each system you want to build, instead of stocking every ingredient at once.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.267D64780256C02B.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.35D42F5BBD5EB46A.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.18E3C9955DF6C3AA.title": "&f&lKeep animal feed in reserve&r",
  "quest.18E3C9955DF6C3AA.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fPlan shelter, breeding supplies and collection around the animals you actually keep. Store animal feed apart from the crop input that the factory consumes.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fLeave safe access for manual care even if parts of the collection become automatic.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.18E3C9955DF6C3AA.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.676C77E188207BE2.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.1E8A78D5D23F7417.title": "&f&lThe Copper irrigation project&r",
  "quest.1E8A78D5D23F7417.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fChapter II includes the frame-based Sprinkler and hydraulic machinery. Follow the installed Sprinkler’s water requirements, then test a small field before expanding.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fInspect water supply and collection when evaluating the field’s performance.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1E8A78D5D23F7417.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 2+",
  "task.709AA0977C3B5C7B.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.7C9363789E53BCEF.title": "&f&lA farm that feeds the sealing line&r",
  "quest.7C9363789E53BCEF.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fConnect wheat and kelp reserves to the water-fed mixer route: one wheat, one kelp and 250 mB water produce two slimeballs. Use the output for Rubber Compound and Copper-tier mechanisms.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fProtect meal ingredients and replanting stock with separate buffers.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.7C9363789E53BCEF.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 2+",
  "task.6FFEB963BB61244F.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.5601454D34EF2835.title": "&f&lFood surplus becomes feedstock&r",
  "quest.5601454D34EF2835.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fChapter VI turns suitable farm output into Mekanism Bio Fuel and the native substrate/ethylene/HDPE chain. Use JEI to choose a supported crop input; keep food-grade output available for people too.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fBegin with the Ender Machine bootstrap equipment before planning Chemical Machine upgrades.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5601454D34EF2835.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 6+",
  "task.673C9D90E1BF97D0.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.0D4CF3C3FC917450.title": "&f&lA kitchen the whole team can use&r",
  "quest.0D4CF3C3FC917450.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBuild a repeatable meal line with ingredient storage, the proper cooking station and finished-food collection. Demonstrate several batches and stock the expedition locker.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fPlace a small manual prep area next to the automated line.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.0D4CF3C3FC917450.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.3EE5FA7764063D70.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.17561A6BE2D911A6.title": "&d◆ &f&lStorage, Backpacks & Collection&r",
  "chapter.17561A6BE2D911A6.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Useful upgrades early · digital storage later"
  ],
  "quest.1C810133157B5A8C.title": "&f&lSort by what you do next&r",
  "quest.1C810133157B5A8C.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fUse named storage for crops, stone, processed metals, mechanisms, tools and expedition loot. Sophisticated Storage and Backpacks add useful upgrades, while ME arrives with Chapter IV.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep an incoming-materials chest so explorers can unload before sorting.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1C810133157B5A8C.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.5F8552A5DD884592.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.345DF7DDC2EBADDE.title": "&f&lA Backpack&r",
  "quest.345DF7DDC2EBADDE.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fObtain a Backpack for supplies and discoveries.",
    "",
    "&fA backpack gives your expeditions a dedicated inventory and upgrade system. Inspect its upgrade slots and tier recipe before adding features.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fLeave a few empty slots for discoveries rather than filling every slot with emergency supplies.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.345DF7DDC2EBADDE.quest_subtitle": "&7ITEM GOAL",
  "quest.144A770BFAD4170E.title": "&f&lThe Hopper Upgrade&r",
  "quest.144A770BFAD4170E.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fObtain and configure a Hopper Upgrade.",
    "",
    "&fA Hopper Upgrade transfers between adjacent inventories using its configuration. It is useful for early machine input and output handling; it does not replace a Pickup Upgrade’s dropped-item job.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fSet filters and test the transfer direction with a small item stack.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.144A770BFAD4170E.quest_subtitle": "&7ITEM GOAL",
  "quest.2D993B872C3B51E0.title": "&f&lThe Pickup Upgrade&r",
  "quest.2D993B872C3B51E0.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fObtain a Backpack Pickup Upgrade and inspect its settings.",
    "",
    "&fUse the Pickup Upgrade for dropped-item collection under its actual range and filter rules. Check the correct storage or backpack variant instead of assuming every upgrade fits both.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest with a few dropped items before relying on it for an entire farm.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.2D993B872C3B51E0.quest_subtitle": "&7ITEM GOAL · TIER 2+",
  "quest.4920B0FADC82FEB2.title": "&f&lKeep the important things&r",
  "quest.4920B0FADC82FEB2.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fFilter what goes into each buffer. Planting stock, tools, boss catalysts and finished mechanisms need different destinations from ordinary overflow.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep your core inventory out of automatic disposal and void-upgrade routes.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.4920B0FADC82FEB2.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.0C5F144195F1F41A.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.6EEBF048369C6E7C.title": "&f&lUpgrade the stored inventory&r",
  "quest.6EEBF048369C6E7C.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fUse the supported tier and upgrade recipes shown in JEI. The managed preserving recipes retain native inventory components; inspect the intended result before upgrading your main container.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest an upgrade on a small spare container first.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.6EEBF048369C6E7C.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.763CB09D010B9068.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.284A2C06A402A811.title": "&f&lStorage that moves&r",
  "quest.284A2C06A402A811.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fThe selected Sophisticated Create integrations support their corresponding contraption inventory features. Test one supported container and transfer arrangement before turning it into a full harvesting system.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fWatch the inventory during movement and when unloading.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.284A2C06A402A811.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.594022165F73CF6A.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.73E65ED5F8E16ACF.title": "&f&lHand off to ME cleanly&r",
  "quest.73E65ED5F8E16ACF.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fWhen Chapter IV opens digital storage, decide which buffers remain local and what moves into ME. Local food, tools and recovery materials are still useful when the network is unavailable.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep a visible reserve for the equipment that restores power or storage access.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.73E65ED5F8E16ACF.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 4+",
  "task.60EAD62A1E0A3AB7.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.6B86EF86C1778977.title": "&d◆ &f&lBuild Your Colony&r",
  "chapter.6B86EF86C1778977.chapter_subtitle": [
    "MineColonies, TownTalk and a factory that supplies the settlement"
  ],
  "quest.14B0B5A57748F8AD.title": "&f&lChoose space for a real town&r",
  "quest.14B0B5A57748F8AD.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fMineColonies has its own building, worker and research progression. Plan a location with room for buildings, roads and later expansion; inspect the native colony guide before placing the first layout.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fPreview buildings and routes before filling the area with machines.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.14B0B5A57748F8AD.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.30BDD600911C9102.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.397BBAD5E08FC694.title": "&f&lThe settlement supply plan&r",
  "quest.397BBAD5E08FC694.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fPrepare the native starting supplies shown in JEI and the colony guide. Keep the first builder’s requested materials in a dedicated buffer so workshop crafting cannot take them unexpectedly.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fChoose a building style whose materials you can gather reliably.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.397BBAD5E08FC694.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.51320ED9CCD34A04.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.3B478246B4568A49.title": "&f&lThe Builder’s Hut&r",
  "quest.3B478246B4568A49.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fObtain a Builder’s Hut and plan its placement.",
    "",
    "&fA builder manages native construction work through its hut and request system. Read the current request and provide the needed materials rather than repeatedly placing new unfinished projects.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fComplete a small first build to learn the colony workflow.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.3B478246B4568A49.quest_subtitle": "&7ITEM GOAL",
  "quest.1EC561905B626291.title": "&f&lHomes, food and work&r",
  "quest.1EC561905B626291.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fA settlement needs housing, food access and suitable jobs according to MineColonies’ native requirements. Grow one manageable neighborhood before creating demand across a huge unfinished town.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fUse the colony screens to check what the citizens actually need.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1EC561905B626291.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.480A7625833A8AC5.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.7CAD3F8890D0644A.title": "&f&lA readable warehouse&r",
  "quest.7CAD3F8890D0644A.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fPlan deliveries and central storage around the colony’s supported warehouse and worker systems. Label the workshop’s supply buffer and avoid sending every rare material to general settlement storage.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fReserve factory catalysts and future-tier materials in a separate secure area.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.7CAD3F8890D0644A.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.102879AF2DEC0F1E.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.1C2AB15EA4CDD5EB.title": "&f&lFollow the colony’s research&r",
  "quest.1C2AB15EA4CDD5EB.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fMineColonies research and building upgrades have their own native conditions. Read the requirement in the colony UI and pursue the next useful service rather than assuming a workshop milestone unlocks it automatically.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fChoose a research goal that solves a current shortage.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.1C2AB15EA4CDD5EB.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.4850E543AC7EB837.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.680A4D3F601E23D4.title": "&f&lConnect one Create supply&r",
  "quest.680A4D3F601E23D4.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fCreate: MineColonies Link supports the selected workshop integration. Follow the installed link’s guidance and test one colony material request from a dedicated Create supply.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fRecord where the request enters and where delivery finishes before expanding.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.680A4D3F601E23D4.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY · TIER 3+",
  "task.759DB06CB422B52C.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.5CD3BA9A76800CD9.title": "&f&lMake the town feel inhabited&r",
  "quest.5CD3BA9A76800CD9.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fTownTalk and the selected colony integrations add character to settlement life. Explore the supported interactions and keep paths, service areas and citizen access clear.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fDesign plazas and practical service routes together rather than decorating over the traffic paths.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.5CD3BA9A76800CD9.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.72CDCA7940B6CB85.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.4C382D373F13242F.title": "&f&lA town ready for trouble&r",
  "quest.4C382D373F13242F.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fFollow the native colony’s guard and defense requirements, secure supply access and leave clear routes through the settlement. Test your own combat away from fragile colony work areas.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep a shared recovery kit and food reserve accessible.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.4C382D373F13242F.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.2B30EE49B21BF3A4.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.0D7964A4C4F74EE5.title": "&f&lA working kingdom district&r",
  "quest.0D7964A4C4F74EE5.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fFinish a district with housing, a useful service, food access and a supplied construction or delivery route. Add signs so a new teammate can understand the town’s organization.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fA smaller finished district is easier to maintain and expand.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.0D7964A4C4F74EE5.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.0391DFCB8C539D99.title": "Complete this activity",
  "chapter.5E8FF85053713AC5.title": "&d◆ &f&lBuilders & Practical Details&r",
  "chapter.5E8FF85053713AC5.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Chipped, Architect’s Palette, Supplementaries and Amendments"
  ],
  "quest.692C289D7B40C0C9.title": "&f&lA building with a clear purpose&r",
  "quest.692C289D7B40C0C9.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fGive each building a job, a palette and room for access. Separate noisy processing, storage, food and magical experiments, then connect them with readable paths.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fUse a limited palette with one accent material so the workshop remains easy to navigate.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.692C289D7B40C0C9.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.008570D50C18EA9C.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.41EAB777014AEBC5.title": "&f&lThe Carpenter’s Table&r",
  "quest.41EAB777014AEBC5.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fObtain a Carpenter’s Table and inspect its decorative options.",
    "",
    "&fChipped workbenches turn supported materials into decorative variants. Inspect which workbench handles your chosen palette and keep these choices distinct from progression frames.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fTest a wall section before producing the entire building palette.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.41EAB777014AEBC5.quest_subtitle": "&7ITEM GOAL",
  "quest.4A5512309A93E914.title": "&f&lArchitect’s Palette in the workshop&r",
  "quest.4A5512309A93E914.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fUnderstand this part of your adventure.",
    "",
    "&fArchitect’s Palette provides building materials and the Algal Blend used by the early industrial route. Decorative variants do not replace the required mechanism or frame in a machine recipe.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fReserve enough kelp and clay for progression before committing them to a large build.",
    "",
    "&7Reading check · Mark this when you understand the guide.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.4A5512309A93E914.quest_subtitle": "&7FIELD GUIDE",
  "task.6A4542ACD3798CC0.title": "Read and understand this guide",
  "quest.618FAF002821E437.title": "&f&lDetails that help people&r",
  "quest.618FAF002821E437.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fSupplementaries and Amendments add practical building and interaction details. Choose actual supported items for signs, lighting, displays or useful room functions by reading their tooltips and recipes.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fA clear label beside an ingredient buffer is a useful part of the build.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.618FAF002821E437.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.722A35AC82DFDE7D.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.60EBE4046B861179.title": "&f&lDesign for maintenance&r",
  "quest.60EBE4046B861179.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fLeave room to reach machine faces, filters, tanks and tool-holding deployers. Add walkways through a factory so expanding a line does not cut off the rest of the building.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fPlan vertical access before stacking a second processing floor.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.60EBE4046B861179.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
  "task.12FFAD3D6BBC5B96.title": "Complete this activity",
  "quest.389D065A21C0981B.title": "&f&lFinish a readable workshop room&r",
  "quest.389D065A21C0981B.quest_desc": [
    "&d&l◆ GOAL&r",
    "&fComplete the project described below.",
    "",
    "&fBuild a room with a consistent palette, visible storage labels, a clear machine flow and safe access to every important input and output.",
    "",
    "&a&l✦ TIP&r",
    "&fKeep the raw-input end and finished-output end recognizable at a glance.",
    "",
    "&7Activity check · Mark this after completing the described project.",
    "",
    "&7Optional branch · Supports your journey alongside the main campaign."
  ],
  "quest.389D065A21C0981B.quest_subtitle": "&7ACTIVITY",
